# steps/named-struct-exec.md, slice 2: a Structure only of fields is executed too -- its fields go back
# to their initializers (Q19.2 = 2: the declarations run again).  Each field is written through its
# path, the Structure is executed, and each reads its initial value -- an int, a char and a size_t.
# A char field takes the reference to its character, so executing writes no character: `other`
# still reads 'z'.  Entry 7.
Point:
    int: x 3
    char: c 'a'
    size_t: z 5U
end: Point
char: other 'z'
Point\x: 8
Point\c: 'z'
Point\z: 6U
int: gx 0
gx: Point\x
Point
int: ax 0
ax: Point\x
char: ac 'q'
ac: Point\c
size_t: az 0U
az: Point\z
int: ok 0
if: gx = 8 && ax = 3 && ac = 'a' && az = 5U && other = 'z'
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
